---
short_label: VII.32
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Any number is either prime or is measured by some prime number.
----
proof:

Let *A* be a number.

I say that *A* either is prime or is measured by some prime number.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="60" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.32 diagram" src="propVII32.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VII.32",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,30;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,30;0;0",
            "A1;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,0;0",
            "A2;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,220,0;0",
            "A;line;connect;A1,A2;black"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

If now *A* is prime, then that which was proposed is done.

But if it is composite, then some prime number measures it. [!just VII.31]

Therefore any number either is prime or is measured by some prime number.

Therefore, *any number is either prime or is measured by some prime number.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide: After the previous proposition, this one really doesn't need to be stated at all.
